sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Browser
    participant JS as app.js
    participant Ctrl as ImageController
    participant Search as ImageSearchService
    participant Repo as ImageRepository

    Note over Browser: user clicks a thumbnail card
    Browser->>Ctrl: GET /image/{id}/modal
    Ctrl->>Search: findById(id)
    Search->>Repo: findSummaryById(id)
    Repo-->>Ctrl: ImageSummary (filename, sheet, cell, tags, description)
    Ctrl-->>Browser: modal HTML fragment -> #modal-content
    Browser->>JS: htmx:afterSwap -> openModal()
    JS-->>Browser: #modal-backdrop gets "open" class

    Note over Browser: user clicks "View Full Image ▶"
    Browser->>Ctrl: GET /image/{id}/viewer
    Ctrl->>Search: getNavigationContext(id)
    Search->>Repo: findFirstId(), findPrevId(id), findNextId(id), findLastId()
    Repo-->>Search: NavigationContext(firstId, prevId, nextId, lastId, id)
    Ctrl->>Search: findById(id)
    Search->>Repo: findSummaryById(id)
    Ctrl-->>Browser: viewer HTML -> #viewer-container<br/>(img src=/image/{id}/bytes, nav buttons<br/>disabled per NavigationContext flags)
    Browser->>JS: htmx:afterRequest -> closeModal()

    Note over Browser: user presses ◀ Prev / Next ▶ / Home / End<br/>(JS maps arrow keys to nav button clicks)
    Browser->>Ctrl: GET /image/{newId}/viewer  (hx-target="#viewer" outerHTML)
    Note right of Ctrl: same flow repeats with newId -<br/>navigation is pure id-ordering,<br/>no stored sort beyond insertion order
